  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Shri Shivam Sengar vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 25 March, 2026 Author: Gurpal Singh Ahluwalia Bench: G. S. Ahluwalia Neutral Citation No. 2026:Mphc-Gwl:10333 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Gwalior Before Hon'Ble Shri Justice G. S. Ahluwalia On The 25th Of March, 2026 Miscellaneous Second Appeal No. 30 of 2025 Shri Shivam Sengar Versus The State Of Madhya Pradesh Appearance:",
    "facts": "2. Facts necessary for disposal of the present appeal, in short, are that on 8/10/2021 at about 6:30 p.m., Collector, Gwalior received a complaint and accordingly on the instructions of Collector, Gwalior, the Food Safety Officer along with his team, went to Platform No.1 of Railway Station, Gwalior where Railway DSP and Tahsildar also met them. It was found that Mava and Paneer were kept on Platform No.1. When it was inquired from NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2026:MPHC-GWL:10333 2 MSA-30-2025 the booking-counter, then it was informed by the Counter in-charge that Mava and Paneer have been booked by Shivam Sengar on his own ID as well as IDs of Pradeep Jain, Hariram Baghel and Manoj Yadav. Accordingly, Tahsildar Kuldeep Dubey, after taking the mobile number of Shivam Sengar from the counter in-charge, called on the mobile number and it was found that Shivam Sengar was already sitting on platform No.1. When Shivam Shri Shivam Sengar vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 25 March, 2026 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/44403211/ 1 Sengar was inquired about Mava and Paneer, then he informed that he has booked the goods for sending it to Bhopal. Accordingly, with the consent of Shivam Sengar, the booking was cancelled and the goods were taken into custody. Thereafter, information was given to Police Station, Padav and accordingly, the police force came and brought Shivam Sengar to police station Padav along with the seized articles. Since the Food Safety Officer was under an apprehension that the Mava and Paneer may be of substandard quality, therefore, the samples were taken with the consent of Shivam Sengar. The total value of the seized goods was Rs.3,76,000/-. The seized articles were sent to the laboratory for report of Food Analyst. As per the report of the Food Analyst, the Mava was found within norms whereas the Paneer was found to be substandard. After receiving the report of the Food Analyst, the copy of report was sent to the applicant to enable him to file an appeal and seek retesting by referral laboratory as provided under section 46(4) of the Act as well as Rule 2.4.2(6) of the Food Safety and Standard Rules, 2011 but no appeal was filed. After completing the investigation, the complaint was filed. 3. Show cause notice was issued by the Adjudicating Officer, but the NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2026:MPHC-GWL:10333 3 MSA-30-2025 applicant did not file any reply and accordingly by order dated 11/4/2023, the right to file reply was closed. The complainant examined Brijesh Kumar Shiromani as PW1 and the Adjudicating Authority, after hearing the parties, held that the applicant is guilty of violation of sections 51 and 58 of the Act and accordingly imposed a penalty of Rs.1,50,000/- for violating section 51 and Rs.50,000/- for violating section 58 of the Act and in total a fine of Rs. two lacs was imposed. 4. Being aggrieved by the order passed by the Adjudicating authority, applicant preferred an appeal which was registered as RCA No. 289/2024 and the Appellate Tribunal, by judgment dated 2/4/2025, dismissed the appeal. 5. Challenging the judgment passed by the Appellate Tribunal, as well as, the order of the Adjudicating Authority, it is submitted by counsel for applicant that the Food Safety Officer was not competent to seize the goods as well as collect samples from Platform No.1 of Railway Station, Gwalior because as per the notification issued in the Official Gazette of India dated 17/6/2021, Shri Om Prakash Sharma was appointed as Food Safety Officer for Western Railway.",
    "arguments": "The only contention of counsel for applicant is that since Shri Om Prakash Sharma NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2026:MPHC-GWL:10333 4 MSA-30-2025 was appointed as the Food Safety Officer for Western Railway, therefore, it has to be presumed that the jurisdiction of the Food Safety Officer was taken away.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "The only contention of counsel for applicant is that since Shri Om Prakash Sharma NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2026:MPHC-GWL:10333 4 MSA-30-2025 was appointed as the Food Safety Officer for Western Railway, therefore, it has to be presumed that the jurisdiction of the Food Safety Officer was taken away.",
